+### Guided pipeline first run
+
+Sets up the prerequisites and supervises one small canary run. The skill
+itself never executes target code: it runs the env checker and (with
+confirmation) the sandbox setup script, then hands the pipeline command to
+the operator to run — or runs it via `bin/vp-sandboxed` only with their
+explicit approval.
+
+**Step A — environment check.** Run `bash scripts/check_env.sh --json` and
+interpret each key (`python`, `docker`, `os`, `gvisor`). On any hard
+failure, print the actionable fix line the script emits and stop — don't
+improvise fixes. Warnings alone are fine to continue past.
+
+**Step B — sandbox provisioning.** If gVisor `runsc` is missing, walk the
+operator through `bash scripts/setup_sandbox.sh`: confirm before running —
+it uses `sudo` and modifies `/etc/docker/daemon.json`. After it completes,
+re-run `bash scripts/check_env.sh` and confirm the `gvisor` check now
+passes (or is still a warn-only miss on non-Linux hosts).
+
+**Step C — model + launch.** Confirm a model is set: `--model` flag or
+`export VULN_PIPELINE_MODEL=<model-id>`. Then, with the operator's
+approval, have them run (or run via `bin/vp-sandboxed` with explicit
+confirmation):
+
+```bash
+bin/vp-sandboxed vuln-pipeline run targets/canary --runs 3 --parallel --stream --max-turns 100
+```
+
+Explain each flag in one line: `--runs 3` = three concurrent find-agents;
+`--parallel` = run them concurrently, round-robin over focus areas;
+`--stream` = judge + reports land as crashes grade, no batch wait;
+`--max-turns 100` = per-agent turn cap so the demo stays cheap.
+
+**Step D — expected outputs.** Describe what lands on disk, exact paths:
+
+- `results/canary/<ts>/found_bugs.jsonl` — each crash as it's found
+- `results/canary/<ts>/run_*/result.json` — per-run grade results
+- `results/canary/<ts>/reports/bug_NN/report.json` — exploitability
+  reports; the first typically lands within minutes, not hours
+
+**Step E — recap.** One-line summary of what the run produced, then point
+at README Step 2 for scaling up (`--runs`, targets) and `docs/pipeline.md`
+for the full operator guide. Offer `/triage` or `/patch` on the results if
+the operator wants to keep going.
 
